ingredients:
  - "1 cup split red lentils (masoor dal)"
  - "2-3 cloves of garlic, minced"
  - "1-inch piece of ginger, grated"
  - "2 green chilies, finely chopped"
  - "Salt to taste"
  - "1 cup chopped spinach"
  - "1 onion, finely chopped"
  - "Ghee for cooking"
instructions:
  - "Soak masoor dal in water for 2-3 hours. Drain and rinse."
  - "Blend the soaked dal with garlic, ginger, green chilies, and salt to make a smooth batter."
  - "Mix in chopped spinach and onions."
  - "Heat a non-stick pan, grease it with ghee, and pour a ladleful of batter."
  - "Spread the batter evenly to make a thin pancake."
  - "Cook until crispy and golden brown on both sides."
  - "Serve hot with your favorite chutney."
